# Package Conventions

## Ownership

Each package has one responsibility. Consult `docs/architecture/package-architecture.md` for
allowed/forbidden dependencies per package.

## UI packages

For `design-tokens`, `ui-web`, and `ui-native` (exports, theme, components, style architecture):
use `.cursor/rules/uiDesignAgent.mdc` and keep `docs/styles/CURRENT-STATE.md` current.

## API package

For `@azes/api` (mutator, Query defaults, auth bridge, facades, OpenAPI consumers):
use `.cursor/rules/apiMenecerAgent.mdc` and keep `docs/api/CURRENT-STATE.md` current.
Codegen / generated-file policy remains `.cursor/rules/api-generation.mdc`.

## Public API

- Consumers import `@azes/<pkg>` or controlled subpaths only.
- Define a package `exports` map. Internals are not importable.
- Never encourage deep imports like `@azes/ui-web/src/components/button/Button`.

## Anti-dumping-ground

- `utils` and `constants` are not junk drawers. New entries need a clear reusable purpose.
- If something is used by exactly one app, keep it in that app.
- Do not create a package to work around a dependency boundary.
- Do not create packages prematurely — only when a phase needs them (`docs/ops/WORKER.md`).

## Framework-agnostic packages

- `design-tokens`, `utils`, `constants`, `types` must not depend on React or React Native.
- No framework-specific code may leak into these packages.

## Before adding a package

1. Confirm it is required by the active approved phase.
2. Document purpose, allowed/forbidden deps, and public API.
3. Prefer extending an existing package over inventing a new one.
